y the armies of the First Crusade, followed by a massacre of many of its inhabitants.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-1187"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (1187)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1187</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 1187 was the recapture of Jerusalem by Saladin after his victory over the Crusaders at Hattin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-587-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (587 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 587 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 587 BCE was the capture and destruction of Jerusalem by the Chaldean (Neo-Babylonian) king Nebuchadnezzar II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-597-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (597 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 597 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 597 BCE was the capture of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar II of the Chaldean Empire after the kingdom of Judah rebelled.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-kawagoe-castle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-kawagoe-castle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Kawagoe Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · Siege · 1545–1546</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Kawagoe Castle was a battle of Japan's Sengoku period in which the Later Hojo clan defended Kawagoe Castle in Musashi province against a large coalition of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-kerman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-kerman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Kerman</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1794</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Kerman was the final siege in 1794 in which the Qajar leader Agha Mohammad Khan captured the city of Kerman from Lotf Ali Khan, the last Zand ruler.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-multan-1818"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Multan (1818)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1818</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Multan in 1818 was the capture of the city of Multan from its Afghan governor by the forces of Ranjit Singh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-odawara-1590"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-odawara-1590.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Odawara (1590)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1590</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Odawara of 1590 was Toyotomi Hideyoshi's campaign against the Later Hojo clan, whose refusal to submit was the last obstacle to his unification of Japan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-orleans"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Orléans</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1428–1429</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Orléans was the English siege of the city of Orléans on the Loire from October 1428 to May 1429, during the Hundred Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-osaka"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-osaka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Osaka</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1614–1615</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Osaka was a series of campaigns in 1614–1615 in which the forces of Tokugawa Ieyasu attacked Osaka Castle, held by the Toyotomi family.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-paris-885-886"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Paris (885–886)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Paris (885–886) was a siege of Paris by a large Viking army.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-pelium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-pelium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Pelium</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 335 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Pelium was fought in 335 BCE when Alexander the Great attacked the Illyrian king Cleitus at the fortress of Pelion on the western border of Macedon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-turin"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-turin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Turin</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1706</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Turin was the French attempt in 1706 to capture the capital of Victor Amadeus II of Savoy during the War of the Spanish Succession.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-tyre-585-572-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Tyre (585–572 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · c. 585 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Tyre was a long siege of the Phoenician island city of Tyre by Nebuchadnezzar II of the Chaldean Empire, begun c. 585 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-urshu"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Urshu</span><span class="enc-type">Siege</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Urshu was a siege by the Hittites of the city of Urshu in northern Syria, recorded in a Hittite text.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-uxellodunum"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Uxellodunum</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 51 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The siege of Uxellodunum in 51 BCE was the last major operation of Julius Caesar's conquest of Gaul.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-vicksburg"><img class="enc-thumb