-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siemowit-iv-of-masovia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siemowit-iv-of-masovia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siemowit IV of Masovia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Siemowit IV of Masovia was a Piast duke of Masovia and a candidate for the Polish throne in 1382.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siemowit-vi-of-masovia"><span class="enc-name">Siemowit VI of Masovia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Siemowit VI of Masovia was a Piast duke who, with his younger brother Władysław II, inherited the lands of Płock, Rawa, Gostynin and other districts of western Masovia…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sieradz-voivodeship"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sieradz-voivodeship.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sieradz Voivodeship</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sieradz Voivodeship was a province of the Kingdom of Poland and the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, formed after the Duchy of Sieradz was incorporated into the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sierra-ecuador"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sierra-ecuador.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sierra (Ecuador)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Sierra is the Andean highland region of Ecuador, formed by two parallel mountain ranges enclosing a series of high basins, with the capital Quito at its northern end.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sierra-de-las-navajas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sierra-de-las-navajas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sierra de las Navajas</span><sp